Kizuki does not bundle or redistribute third-party source code in this
repository. Its direct runtime dependencies are resolved from the npm registry
at install time and remain under their own licenses:

  - ai, @ai-sdk/openai-compatible  (Apache-2.0)  https://github.com/vercel/ai
  - workflow                       (Apache-2.0)  https://github.com/vercel/workflow
  - next                           (MIT)         https://github.com/vercel/next.js
  - react, react-dom               (MIT)         https://github.com/facebook/react
  - better-sqlite3                 (MIT)         https://github.com/WiseLibs/better-sqlite3
  - sqlite-vec                     (MIT OR Apache-2.0)  https://github.com/asg017/sqlite-vec
  - unpdf                          (MIT)         https://github.com/unjs/unpdf
  - fast-xml-parser                (MIT)         https://github.com/NaturalIntelligence/fast-xml-parser
  - fflate                         (MIT)         https://github.com/101arrowz/fflate
  - zod                            (MIT)         https://github.com/colinhacks/zod

The published npm package includes the built app (.next/), which contains
compiled code from these dependencies under their own licenses. The only
copyleft code in the dependency tree is sharp's prebuilt libvips binary
(LGPL-3.0-or-later), which Next.js loads unmodified as a separate library for
image handling.
